Implement External SSL Certificate Renewal Automation

Objective

Automate the current external certificate renewal process using TeamCity, DigiCert, NSX-ALB and Fastly while retaining SysAdmin approval and billing ownership.




Story 1 — Parameterize the existing TeamCity certificate workflow

Description

Extend or clone the existing Maintenance / NSX-ALB Certificate Issue configuration for external certificate renewal.

Tasks

Add operation parameter:
Renew
Reissue
NewOrder
DeployOnly
Add certificate CN and SAN parameters.
Add DigiCert order ID or certificate ID.
Add NSX-ALB certificate-template identifier.
Add NSX-ALB Virtual Service identifier.
Add Fastly-routed boolean.
Add Fastly TLS certificate/domain identifier.
Add dry-run mode.
Add secure API credential references.
Preserve existing internal certificate behavior.

Acceptance criteria

Renewal and new-order paths are clearly differentiated.
TeamCity validates required parameters before execution.
Existing internal workflow is not broken.
No private keys are written to build logs or normal artifacts.
Story 2 — Automate NSX-ALB CSR generation and certificate discovery

Description

Reuse the existing TeamCity and NSX-ALB process to generate the CSR from the private key stored in NSX-ALB and identify all related certificate objects.

Tasks

Find the current NSX-ALB certificate/template by CN or UUID.
Capture the current certificate metadata.
Capture the current Virtual Service binding.
Generate or retrieve the CSR using the existing private key.
Validate CSR CN and SANs.
Publish only the CSR as a TeamCity artifact.
Record the current certificate for rollback.

Acceptance criteria

CSR is generated from the intended NSX-ALB certificate object.
Private key remains protected in NSX-ALB.
CN and SANs are verified before submission.
Current Virtual Service binding is recorded.
Story 3 — Automate DigiCert renewal and certificate retrieval

Description

Automate the normal renewal path against the existing DigiCert order.

Tasks

Locate the latest DigiCert order for the domain.
Confirm the order is eligible for renewal.
Submit the renewal using the generated CSR.
Apply the correct product and term.
Use the new invoice/account-balance workflow.
Record SysAdmin approval status.
Poll the DigiCert order until issued.
Download the certificate and chain.
Handle pending approval, validation, rejection and timeout states.

Acceptance criteria

The workflow renews an existing certificate rather than creating a new order by default.
SysAdmin approval remains a controlled dependency.
Issued certificate and chain are retrieved automatically.
DigiCert order and request IDs are captured for audit purposes.
Story 4 — Automate NSX-ALB certificate import and Virtual Service update

Description

Complete the NSX-ALB portion after DigiCert issues the renewed certificate.

Tasks

Locate the temporary certificate template containing the private key.
Import the renewed certificate.
Validate the certificate and key match.
Create or update the final application certificate object.
Follow the required naming convention.
Preserve the old certificate until validation succeeds.
Update the target Virtual Service SSL certificate binding.
Verify the new certificate is selected and the old one is removed only when safe.
Save and re-query the configuration.

Acceptance criteria

Renewed certificate is successfully combined with the existing private key.
Target Virtual Service references the new certificate.
Previous certificate remains available for rollback.
The endpoint presents the new certificate after the update.
Story 5 — Automate conditional Fastly certificate replacement

Description

When the domain is listed as Fastly-routed, deploy the renewed certificate and key to Fastly after the NSX-ALB step.

Tasks

Maintain a managed list or mapping of Fastly-routed domains.
Export or securely obtain the private key from NSX-ALB.
Prevent the key from appearing in TeamCity logs or retained artifacts.
Find the existing Fastly TLS certificate.
Replace the certificate and key.
Preserve the existing TLS activation.
Validate both the primary and www hostname.
Remove unused private keys only after successful deployment.

Acceptance criteria

Fastly deployment executes only for mapped Fastly domains.
Certificate and key are replaced through API.
Existing activation remains functional.
The public endpoint presents the expected renewed certificate.
Story 6 — Add validation, rollback and reporting

Description

Make live endpoint validation—not API upload success—the final success criterion.

Tasks

Run OpenSSL or an equivalent TLS inspection.
Capture:
Serial number
Expiration date
Issuer
SANs
Thumbprint
Compare the live certificate with the DigiCert-issued artifact.
Validate the NSX-ALB endpoint.
Validate the Fastly endpoint when applicable.
Restore the previous Virtual Service binding if NSX-ALB validation fails.
Retain or restore the previous Fastly certificate if external validation fails.
Publish TeamCity status.
Notify Teams/Jira.

Acceptance criteria

Pipeline succeeds only after live validation passes.
Rollback steps are documented and testable.
Failures identify the affected domain, certificate and deployment target.
Results are auditable.
Story 7 — Pilot the internal NSX-ALB automation

This should be your first practical test.

Objective

Use the existing TeamCity script with a low-risk internal certificate to automate issuance, NSX-ALB import, Virtual Service update and validation.

Tasks

Select a non-production or low-risk internal Virtual Service.
Clone the existing TeamCity job.
Run discovery and CSR generation in dry-run mode.
Issue a SILAC CA certificate using the existing internal process.
Automate NSX-ALB certificate import.
Automate Virtual Service certificate binding.
Validate with OpenSSL.
Test rollback.
Document gaps before connecting DigiCert and Fastly.

Why this pilot makes sense

It tests the hardest reusable infrastructure pieces first:

TeamCity orchestration
NSX-ALB authentication
Certificate object discovery
Private-key handling
Certificate import
Virtual Service update
Validation
Rollback

You can prove those without waiting for DigiCert billing and SysAdmin approval.

Story 8 — Pilot one external DigiCert renewal

After the internal pilot succeeds:

Select one approved low-risk external domain.
Generate CSR from NSX-ALB.
Renew its existing DigiCert order.
Complete SysAdmin approval.
Import the certificate back into NSX-ALB.
Update the Virtual Service.
Deploy to Fastly if routed through Fastly.
Validate both origin/internal and public endpoints.
Document production-readiness findings.













